# BioIntel AI 15.6.0 - Step217 Production Enablement Controls on Step206 Windows V19.6

BioIntel AI is a Windows-first, local-first professional bioinformatics and biomedical AI platform developed by Lavesh Dobriyal.

**Biology, Engineered into Intelligence.**

## Step217 production-enablement upgrade

Step217 adds qualified-engine-only pipeline execution, nine priority native
workflow contracts, Ed25519 signed archive verification, enterprise backend
adapters, OIDC/JWKS verification, FHIR/DICOMweb/REDCap/LIMS connectors,
qualification-gated vector RAG and a cleaner Operational/Platform/Assurance/Internal
module catalogue.

Run VERIFY_STEP217_PRODUCTION_ENABLEMENT_WINDOWS.bat after extracting all five
matching Parts. The software-control gate passes only when the Step217 code,
configuration, navigation and safety policies are complete. The separate
production-evidence gate remains blocked until exact engines, authentic model
weights, enterprise credentials, publisher certificates and independent
scientific evidence are supplied.
## Step216 release-readiness upgrade

Step216 adds a software readiness and metadata assurance layer on top of the
existing Step206 five-part Windows package and Step215 Engine Platform
integration. The physical installer contract, LocalAppData managed install path,
offline CPython 3.11 wheelhouse and UserData-preserving recovery controls remain
unchanged.

After extracting all five matching ZIP parts, you can run
`VERIFY_STEP216_RELEASE_READINESS_WINDOWS.bat` to verify release metadata,
source-manifest compatibility, wheelhouse presence, documentation, recovery
controls and qualification boundaries without launching external engines.

## Supported Windows workflow

After extracting all five matching Step206 ZIP parts into one new folder, use only:

1. `INSTALL_WINDOWS.bat`
2. `RUN_BOTH_WINDOWS.bat`

The installer verifies all four parts, the active SHA-256 source manifest, the bundled offline wheelhouse, compatible CPython 3.11.x x64, managed LocalAppData installation, database backup/migration, and a native Windows UI/API/worker startup-and-shutdown smoke test. It refreshes stable Desktop and Start Menu shortcuts so the installed app no longer depends on the extracted download folder.

`RUN_BOTH_WINDOWS.bat` uses a resident supervisor with strict API, Streamlit, local SQLite read/write and worker readiness checks. Startup failure cleans all owned processes and creates sanitized diagnostics. Ollama, SearXNG and external providers remain optional and isolated from the offline core.

See `CURRENT_RELEASE.md`, `CHANGELOG_STEP206_WINDOWS_INSTALL_RUN.md` and `RELEASE_TEST_REPORT_STEP206.md`. Step205 scientific upgrade records remain available for provenance.

Historical provenance includes Step 159 runtime-resilience foundations and later release gates; Step206 is the active release.

## Step206 V19.6 professional hardening

V19.6 retains the complete V19.1–V19.5 scientific, collaboration and engine-platform work. The ultimate professional hardening adds canonical repair/diagnose/safe-mode/uninstall controls, a central 269-entry product registry, reproducible module/engine/model/reference exports, sanitized diagnostics, UserData-preserving recovery and a stricter five-part release gate. Run `INSTALL_WINDOWS.bat` from the newly extracted V19.6 package before `RUN_BOTH_WINDOWS.bat`.

After installation, `RUN_ULTIMATE_ACCEPTANCE_WINDOWS.bat` performs the final target-machine software qualification and writes its evidence under the dedicated UserData reports directory.

Step216 is not clinical authorization, regulatory validation, wet-lab
validation, model-weight qualification or external-engine qualification.
External engines remain unqualified until exact artifact, licence, checksum and
target-machine evidence passes.
